    "method": "Land area is California's 30x30 ecoregion land grid (resolution-10 H3 cells, about 3.7 acres each), the same definition of California the 30x30 program uses; a region's land is the grid cells inside it. Each cell's conservation status is its share in GAP 1–2 and GAP 3–4 from the 2025 30x30 Conserved Areas inventory; because a conserved-area unit's GAP percentages are not mapped within the unit, the unit's split is applied evenly across it — the report's 'proportional estimate'. Land outside every conserved-area unit is non-conserved. Statewide this reproduces the report's 26.1% / 25.5% / 48.4% to within 0.2 points."
